hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2806","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja`far narrated to us, saying: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Minhal. Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his uncle, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Aslam: “Fast today.” They said: We had already eaten. He said: “Fast.” for the rest of your day,” meaning the day of Ashura, the opposite of which is happy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2807","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Khuza`i, on the authority of his uncle, They went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning on the day of Ashura, and they had been exhausted from lunch, so he said to them: “Have you fasted today?” he said. We said, “We have finished lunch.” So he ordered us to complete the rest of our day. Or he said to them, “Complete the rest of your day.”"
"2808","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Salamah. Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his uncle, said: We went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the morning of Ashura, and he said to us: “Have you been fasting in the morning?” We said. We have had lunch, O Messenger of God. He said: “So fast for the rest of your day.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Bakr is not strong in hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2809","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abu Sufyan, saying: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Ashura, saying: “I am fasting, so whoever wants, let him fast,” and he sent to the people of Al-Awali, and he said: “Whoever has eaten, let him not eat, and whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This last statement is not a mistake. We know of one of the companions of al-Zuhri. I heard Qutaibah speak against him and oppose him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2810","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Muawiyah, on the day of Ashura While he was on the pulpit in the city, he said: Where are your scholars, O people of the city? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on this day: “I am fasting, so whoever among you wants to fast, let him fast.” Abu Abdul Rahman: This is more likely to be correct than the hadith of Muhammad bin Mansour, and the other statement is wrong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2811","I read about Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Aidh, who said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf said: I heard Muawiyah, and he went up to this pulpit and said: Where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on this day: “This is the day of Ashura, and God has not prescribed for you to fast it, and I He is fasting, so whoever among you likes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever dislikes it, let him abandon it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake. We do not know that One of the companions of Al-Zuhri said something other than this in this hadith, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and the correct opinion is Humaid bin Abdul Rahman. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2812","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard al-Numan talking, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid said: He heard Muawiyah giving a sermon from the pulpit of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O people of Medina, I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “This is the day of Ashura, and fasting on it has not been made obligatory for you, while I am fasting. So whoever likes to fast, let him fast, and whoever He likes to break the fast, so let him break the fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is also a mistake, and al-Nu’man ibn Rashid made many mistakes, on the authority of al-Zuhri, And his counterpart is in Al-Zuhri, and with him is Ibn Salih. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2813","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Yaqoub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman told him He heard Muawiyah addressing the people in Medina, saying: O people of Medina, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “This is the day of Ashura, and God has not prescribed for you to fast it, but I am fasting. Muawiyah said that, so whoever likes to fast, let him fast, and whoever likes to break his fast, let him break his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And this is it. The right thing"
"2814","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad reported, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Mawhib, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Ibn Sundar, on the authority of men among them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man who had converted to Islam after the morning of Ashura: “Go to your people and tell them to fast this day.” Al-Aslami said: O Messenger of God, have you seen if you find any of them? Did you have lunch? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let him complete his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2815","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Amr bin Ghallab told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj told me, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas in the Sacred Mosque, and I asked him about fasting on Ashura. He said: Prepare, so when you wake up on the ninth day, start fasting. I said: “This is how Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast?” He said: Yes, this is how he used to fast. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2816","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Yahya bin Hassan told us, saying: He said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, saying: Yahya bin Al-Harith told me On the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting the month of Ramadan is equivalent to ten months.” And fasting for six days during two months is fasting for a year.”"
"2817","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, he said: Yahya bin Al-Harith told me, he said: Abu told me Asma Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “God made A good deed is for ten months, a month is for ten months and six days after breaking the fast, the completion of the year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2818","Ahmad bin Yahya reported, saying: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Hassan, who is Ibn Salih, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr Al-Laythi, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it... With six days of Shawwal, he has fasted the whole year.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong, but the correct thing is Omar bin Thabit. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2819","Khallad bin Aslam reported, Al-Darawardi said: On the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, and Saad bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted an entire eternity.”"
"2820","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam reported, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Warqa’, on the authority of Sa’d bin Sa’id, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted a lifetime.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sa’d bin Sa’id is weak. Likewise, Ahmad bin Hanbal said, and they were three brothers: Yahya bin Sa’id bin Qays. Al-Ma'mun is one of the imams, trustworthy, and Abd Rabbuh bin Sa'id has no problem with him, and Sa'd bin Sa'id is the third of them, weak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2821","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah bin al-Hajjaj narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, that he said: “Whoever fasts the month of Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal, as if he had fasted the entire year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2822","Hisham bin Ammar reported on the authority of Sadaqa bin Khaled, he said: Utbah told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr told me, he said: he told me Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, said: We attacked with Abu Ayyub, so he fasted Ramadan and we fasted, so when we broke his fast, he rose among the people, and said “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ‘Whoever fasts Ramadan and fasts six days of Shawwal, it will be as if he fasted for a lifetime.’” Abu Abdul Rahman: This Utba bin Abi Al-Hakam is not strong. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza al-Harrani reported, saying: Uthman, who is the son of Amr Al-Harrani, he said: Omar, meaning Ibn Thabit, told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This sheikh has books other than this, so his hadiths are similar to the hadiths of Muhammad bin Abi Humaid. He said: I do not know. Was he hearing it from Muhammad or was he hearing it from those sheikhdoms? As for the Sheikh, he used to tell us about him, and he did not mention Muhammad bin Abi Humaid, so if those hadiths were his hadiths about those sheikhs He did not hear it from Muhammad, for he is weak, meaning Uthman, and Muhammad bin Abi Humayd is nothing in the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2823","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, saying: Abd al-Ala told us, saying: Hammad told us, saying: Thabit reported, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran, and Sa`id. Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran, who is Ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “Did Did you fast anything during the month of Sha`ban?” He said: No. He said: “Then if you break your fast, fast for two days.” Al-Jariri said: Then fast."
"2824","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Have you fasted anything during this month?” He said: No. He said: “Then you break your fast, or he breaks your fast.” People should fast for two days.” Amr said: Yahya told us twice, once on the authority of anecdote that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Imran. Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Ibn Abi Adi reported, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran, and the like. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Al-Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu al-Ala’ ibn al-Shakhir narrated to us, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to us. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to a man: He reminded him of something similar. I said: Who is Abu Al-Ala telling this about? He said: I asked a man from his family about whom was this Abu Al-Ala speaking to? The man said: On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2825","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Da’eef told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said “I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasting during the ten days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2826","Amr bin Yazid reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “never fasted for ten days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2827","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim reported, saying: Abu Nu`aym told us, saying: Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: “I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasting on the ten days of prayer.”"
"2828","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Hamza Al-Aslami, that he saw a man He followed people’s journeys to Mina on the days of Tashreeq on a camel, saying: “Don’t you fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. Abdullah bin Abi Bakr and Salem Abu Al-Nadr disagreed with him."
"2829","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim Abi al-Nadr, and Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hudhafah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded him to announce on the days of Tashreeq that they are"
"2830","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade fasting during the days of Mina.” Bakr ibn al-Ashjaj related it with a difference of opinion from his son and Amr regarding it."
"2831","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Makhramah ibn Bukayr, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar that Al-Hakam heard Al-Zarqi say: My mother told me that they were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mina, and they heard a passenger screaming, saying: “ “Isn’t anyone fasting, for these are days of eating and drinking?” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not know that anyone followed Makhramah on this hadith. On the authority of Al-Hakam Al-Zarqi, and the correct one is Masoud bin Al-Hakam"
"2832","Ahmad ibn al-Haytham told us, he said: Harmala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr told me, that Bukayr told him, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Yasar, that Masoud Ibn Al-Hakam told him, on the authority of his mother, who said: A rider passed by us while we were in Mina with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, calling. Among the people: “Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.” My sister said: This is Ali bin Abi Talib. I said: Rather, he is So-and-so mentioned disagreement with Al-Zuhri"
"2833","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Muammar reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Masoud ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abdullah bin Hudhafa to ride his camel for a few days.” From Mina, people shouted: “No one should fast, for these are days of eating and drinking.” He said: I saw him on his mount calling for that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2834","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, saying: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Masoud bin Al-Hakam said: Some people told me The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported that: He saw Abdullah bin Hudhafah while he was walking on his camel during the days of the Tashreeq, calling out to the people of Mina: “Don’t No one should fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking. It was reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him as a herald. “With that in them.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Zuhri did not hear Ibn Masoud ibn al-Hakam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2835","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Homsi reported, saying: Ahmad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he had heard that Masoud ibn al-Hakam was He narrates, on the authority of some of their scholars among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He sent Abdullah bin Hudhafa to tour the people of Mina on A red she-camel, saying: “No one will fast these days, for these are the days of eating, drinking, and remembering God.”"
"2836","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani reported, he said: Ruh told us, he said: Saleh told us, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abdullah to go around Mina to tell you not to fast these days. For these are the days of eating, drinking, and remembering God.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Saleh is Ibn Abi al-Akhdar, and this hadith of his is wrong. He is much in error on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and his counterpart is Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa, and both of them are weak, and Ruh ibn Ubadah is not strong according to us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2837","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a reading on his behalf, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he greeted: He sent Abdullah bin Hudhafah, saying: These are the days of eating and drinking and remembrance of God, meaning the days of Mina. Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: This hadith was narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Yusuf bin Masoud bin Al-Hakam"
"2838","Issa bin Hammad bin Zugha told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Yusuf bin Masoud bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of His grandmother said: While we were in Mina, a passenger arrived and I heard him calling, “These are the days of eating and drinking during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” May God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Who is this? He said: Ali bin Abi Talib. The disagreement over Ibn Ishaq was mentioned in this hadith."
"2839","Imran bin Bakkar al-Homsi reported, saying: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, saying: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam Al-Zarqi, he said: My mother told me, she said: It is as if I am looking at Ali bin Abi Talib on the mule of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Bayda when he rose up against the Ansar people, saying: O community of Muslims, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “These are not days “Fasting, these are days of eating and drinking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2840","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah told me Ibn Abi Salamah, on the authority of Masoud Ibn Al-Hakam, on the authority of his mother, that she told him, she said: It is as if I am looking at Ali Ibn Abi Talib while he is on The white mule of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood over the Ansar people, and he was saying: O people, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “These are not days of fasting, but rather days of eating, drinking, and remembrance.”"
"2841","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: Someone told me, who heard Abdullah bin Abu Salamah, and I did not see it except that I heard it from him narrating, on the authority of Masoud ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of his mother, she said: It is as if I am looking at Ali ibn Abi A student riding on the white mule of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: O people, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “The The days of Tashreeq are days of eating and drinking, not days of fasting.” Ibn al-Haad disagreed with this (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2842","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym al-Zarqi, On the authority of his mother, she said: While we were in Mina, Ali bin Abi Talib was riding a camel, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The These are days of eating and drinking, so no one should fast because of disagreement over a lover."
"2843","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, who is Al-Masoudi, told us, he said: Habib bin Abi told me Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Bishr bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out During the days of the Tashreeq, he said: “No one will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul. Indeed, these days are about eating and drinking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2844","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Bishr bin Suhaim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech during the days of Hajj, and he said: “No one will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and these are days \Eating and drinking\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2845","Yusuf bin Isa reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, he said: Yazid, who is the son of Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, reported on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Bishr bin Suhaim said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit, saying: “No one will enter Paradise except a Muslim, and this The days of eating and drinking, the days of Tashreeq.”"
"2846","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Abu Al-Nu’man Al-Hakam bin Abdullah told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Habib, saying: I heard Nafi’ Ibn Jubayr narrates, on the authority of Bishr Ibn Suhaim, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded him to announce the days of Tashreeq that they are days of eating.” And drink, and that no one will enter Paradise except a believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2847","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of a man among the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Bishr bin Suhaym and ordered him to proclaim: “Indeed, he will not enter Paradise except A believing soul, and these are the days of eating and drinking, meaning the days of the sunrise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2848","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Bishr bin Suhaim, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, “He commanded him to announce the days of sunrise, saying that no one will enter Paradise except a believer, and they are days of eating and drinking.” Qutayba bin Saeed reported it again, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Nafi’, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave the order of a herald, As a messenger, Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Dawud told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a man who was called: “Tidings of good tidings in the days of Mina gave the call to prayer, and the hadith was narrated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2849","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Muammar narrated, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Muttalib, he said: He invited an Arab to his meal. That was the day after the Day of Sacrifice. The Bedouin said: I am fasting. He said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “It is forbidden to fast on these days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2850","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Kathir, on the authority of Ja`far ibn al-Muttalib, that Abdullah ibn Amr, he entered upon Amr ibn al-Aas while he was having lunch, and said: Come, and he said: I am fasting, then he entered upon him again, and said: Come, He said: I am fasting. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These are the days of eating and drinking,” meaning the days of Tashreeq. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2851","Ahmad ibn Bakkar informed me, saying: Mukhlid informed us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed me, saying: Sa`id ibn Kathir informed me, that Ja`far ibn al-Muttalib He told him that Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas came to see Amr bin Al-Aas during the days of Mina and invited him to lunch, and he said: I am fasting, then The second and likewise, then the third, and he said: No, unless I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “For I heard it from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"2852","Ahmad bin Abdah reported, saying: Husayn, who is Al-Ashqar, told us, saying: Sharik told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Sulaym, he is Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The days of Tashreeq are days of eating and drinking.” And a prayer that no one fasts.” Ibrahim bin Muhajir disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2853","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Husayn Al-Ju’fi told me, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’a’a, On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These are the days of taste and remembrance,” meaning the days of Tashreeq."
"2854","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan. Al-Bajli, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “The best fast after the month of Ramadan is a month you call Muharram.”"
"2855","Muhammad ibn Qudamah reported, saying: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Humaid ibn Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, raised it, and said: “The best fast after the month of Ramadan is God’s month of Muharram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2856","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Zaida told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, On the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which prayer is better after the obligatory prayer? He said: “Praying in the middle of the night.” It was said: Which fast is better after Ramadan? He said: “The month of God which you call Muharram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2857","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best fast after the month of Ramadan is the month of God’s Muharram.”"
"2858","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He fasts to the point that we say: He does not break the fast, and he breaks the fast to the point that we say: He does not fast, and I have never seen him fast in a month more than in Sha`ban. He used to fast during the month of Sha`ban except \Rather"," he used to fast the entire month of Sha'ban.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2859","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da’eef told us, he said: Zaid, who is Ibn al-Hubab, told us, he said: Nuh bin Abi Bilal told me, he said: Zaid bin Abi told me Reproach, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, who said: I asked Aisha about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “It was Most of his fasting after the month of Ramadan is the entire month of Sha`ban or all of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2860","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, that Abdullah bin Abi Qays told him, that He heard Aisha say: “The most beloved of the months to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to fast in Sha`ban, which he used to connect with Ramadan.”"
"2861","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad reported, saying: Muhammad ibn Rabi`ah told us, on the authority of Abu Umays, whose name is Utba ibn Abdullah, on the authority of al-Alaa ibn Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the middle of Sha`ban comes, stop fasting,” he said. Abu Abd al-Rahman: We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith other than Al-Ala bin Abd al-Rahman. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2862","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abthar, who is Ibn al-Qasim Kufi, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother died and she had to fast for a month. Should I fast on her behalf? He said: “What do you think, if she had a debt, would you have paid it off?” He said: Yes. He said: “The debt of God is more deserving of being repaid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2863","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, saying: Husayn bin Ali Al-Ju’fi told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sulayman Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my mother died and she had to fast for a month. Should I make up for it? About her? He said: “If your mother had a debt, would you have paid it off on her behalf?” He said: Yes, he said: “The debt of God is more deserving of being paid.” Solomon said: Then the arbitrator said, And Salama bin Kuhail, while we were all sitting, where Muslim narrated this hadith, and they said: We heard Mujahid mention it on the authority of Ibn Abbas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2864","Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Salamah, Al-Hakam, and Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, Ata’ and Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My sister died and she must fast. Two months in a row. He said: “What do you think, if your sister owed a debt, would you have repaid it?” She said: Yes. He said: “Then God’s rights are more worthy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2865","Al-Hussein bin Mansour Al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mughra’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a woman came to him and said: My mother died and she had to fast for a month. Should I make up for it? About her? He said: “What do you think, if she had a debt, would you have paid it off?” She said: Yes. He said: “The debt of God is more deserving of being paid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2866","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith narrated, saying: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ayan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother died and she had to fast for a month. Should I pay it off on her behalf? He said: “Do you think that if she had a debt, would you have paid it off? God’s debt is more deserving that she should pay it off.” Suleiman said: Salama told him Ibn Kuhayl, and a similar ruling on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2867","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar narrated, saying: Zakaria bin Adi narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated, on the authority of Zaid, saying: Al-Hakam narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother died and she must fast. A vow, should I fast from it? He said: “Would you have repaid your mother’s debt if she had owed it?” She said: Yes. He said: “Then fast on behalf of your mother.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He narrated Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: No one should fast on behalf of someone else."
"2868","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, told us, saying: Hajjaj al-Ahwal told us, saying: Ayoub bin Musa told us, On the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “No one should pray on behalf of another, and no one should fast on behalf of another, but he should feed on his behalf in place of him.” A mud of wheat every day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2869","Ali bin Uthman al-Harrani al-Nufaili and Ismail bin Yaqoub al-Harrani al-Subaihi reported, saying: Ibn Musa, who is Muhammad bin Musa bin Ayn Al-Harrani said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, that Muhammad bin Ja’far told him, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies and is obligated to fast, his guardian will fast on his behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2870","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Yahya bin Saeed and Abd al-Rahman told me, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Othman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should not fast while her husband is present unless \With His permission\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2871","Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for a woman to fast while her husband is a witness, except with his permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2872","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf reported, Al-Awza’i said: On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Was I not informed that you fast during the day and stay awake at night?” I said: Yes, O Messenger. God said: “So do not do that. Fast and break your fast, sleep and get up, for your soul has a right over you, your body has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. Indeed, it is sufficient for you to fast three days of every month, for a good deed is multiplied ten times its value, so that is fasting for an entire lifetime.” So I strengthened myself, and he stressed me out. I said: O Messenger of God, I am finding strength. He said: “Then fast for three days every Friday.” So I strengthened myself, and he stressed me out. I said: O Messenger of God, I am finding strength. He said: “Fast as the Prophet of God David did, and do not add to it.” I said: O Messenger of God, and what is fasting? David said: “Half an eternity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2873","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri narrated on the authority of Yazid, who was Ibn Zurai’, who said: Husayn al-Mu’allim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi narrated to us. Many, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and said: Was I not told that you would stay up at night and fast during the day? I said: Yes. He said: Do not do that. Get up and sleep, and fast and break your fast, for your body is upon you. Indeed, your eye has a right over you, your visitor has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you, and it is sufficient for you that you fast from every A month is three days, and for every good deed you will get ten times more.” So I stressed, and he stressed to me. I said: I am able to do anything other than that. He said: “So fast from Every Friday for three days.” So I stressed, and he stressed on me. I said: I am able to do anything other than that. He said: “Fast the fast of the Prophet of God, David.” I said: And what is fasting? God’s prophet David? He said: “Half an eternity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2874","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja`dah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr al-Qari, He said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: “No, by the Lord of this House. I did not say: Whoever is caught in the morning while he is junub, then Muhammad should not fast. By God “The Kaaba,” he said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2875","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik reported, saying: Bishr ibn Shuaib told us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd informed me. Allah ibn Umar said that he had a wet dream at night during Ramadan and woke up before dawn came, then he fell asleep before he took a bath and did not wake up until In the morning, he said: I met Abu Hurairah in the morning and asked him for a fatwa about that, and he said: Break your fast, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had He used to order people to break the fast when a man was junub in the morning.” Abdullah bin Abdullah said: “I came to Abdullah bin Omar and mentioned to him the one who had given me a fatwa.” Abu Hurairah did so, and he said: I swear to God, if you break your fast, it will cause pain to your youth. Fast, but if it seems to you that you should fast another day, then do otherwise. Aqeel bin Khalid narrated it on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2876","Abdul-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar told me that he had a wet dream at night during Ramadan, and he woke up before dawn, then fell asleep before dawn. He took a bath and did not wake up until the morning. He said: I met Abu Hurairah in the morning and asked him for a fatwa, and he said: You break your fast, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to order people to break the fast when a man was junub in the morning. Ubayd Allah said: So I came to Abdullah and mentioned to him the fatwa that Abu Hurairah, and he said: I swear to God, if you break your fast, I will cause pain to your youth. If you wish to fast another"
"2877","Ahmad bin Uthman and Muawiyah bin Salih told me, they said: Khalid told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Umair, told us, he said: I heard Al-Maqbari says: Abu Hurairah used to give fatwas to the people stating that whoever becomes junub should not fast that day, so Aisha sent to him: No. He spoke about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, like this: “I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was junub in the morning. from his family, then he fasts.” He said: Ibn Abbas told him."
"2878","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, On the authority of his brother Muhammad, that he used to hear Abu Hurairah say: “Whoever has a wet dream at night or has intercourse with his family, then dawn overtakes him, and he does not He takes a bath and does not fast. He said: Then I heard him stop doing that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2879","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Yazid told us, saying: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Raja’ bin Haywa, saying: Ya’la bin Uqba built With his wife during Ramadan, and in the morning he was junub, he asked Abu Hurairah and he said: Should I break my fast? He said: Should I not fast this day and reward him with another day? His place? He said: No, so Marwan came and mentioned that to him, so he sent Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham to Aisha and asked her. Regarding that, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning when he was in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, so he would bathe, then he would become fasting in the morning. He said: With it, Abu Hurairah said: My neighbor is my neighbor. He said: I bequeathed that you meet him. So I met him and narrated the hadith to him. He said: I did not hear it from anyone. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only Al-Fadl ibn Abbas told me about that. I said to Raja’: Who told you about Ali? He said: It was narrated to me by Ali. And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about this hadith. Marwan reported that Abu Hurairah narrates, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He acknowledged that he had said: “Whoever finds himself in the morning while he is junub must not fast that day,” so he sent to Aisha to ask her about that, so I set off. With him, he asked her, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then fast that day.” So he returned to Marwan spoke to him, and he said: Meet Abu Hurairah, and he spoke to him, and he said: He is my neighbor, and I hate to receive him as he dislikes, so he said to him I invite you to teach him. They said: He met him and told him. He said: Al-Fadl told me. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Omar bin Abi Bakr disagreed with them. Ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated it, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Usama ibn Zaid (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2880","Ja`far bin Musafir reported, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Aisha told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out in the morning and his head was dripping with water. Marriage without a dream, then fasting in the morning. Abdul Rahman mentioned this to Marwan bin Al-Hakam, and Marwan said: I swear to you that you will not go. To Abu Hurairah, I told him this. Abdul Rahman said: May God forgive you. He is a friend of mine, and I do not like to respond to what he said, and he was Abu Hurairah said: “Whoever has a wet dream during the night or has an intercourse, then dawn overtakes him and he has not washed himself, then he must not fast.” Marwan said: I have determined for you not to I went, so Abdul Rahman went and told him that. Abu Hurairah said: She is more knowledgeable about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than we are. Usama bin Zaid told me about that. He said: Abu Abdul Rahman. Abu Hazim Marwan bin Jurayj disagreed over Abdul Malik bin Abi. A virgin in it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2881","Amr bin Ali reported, on the authority of Fudayl bin Sulaiman, who said: Abu Hazim told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of his father, said: I was with Abdul-Rahman at Marwan’s house, and they mentioned that Abu Hurairah said: “Who He had a wet dream and knew that he had a wet dream and did not wash himself until morning, so he should not fast that day. He said: Go and ask the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello to that, so he went and I went with him until he came to Aisha and greeted Aisha at the door, and said: A man has a wet dream and he is aware of his wet dream. So he does not wash until the morning. Will he fast that day? Aisha said: O Abdul Rahman, do you not have a good example in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, she said: For I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he would wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then fast. That day.” Then I went out until I came to Umm Salamah, and he said to her: As he said to Aisha, and she said: To me, as Aisha said, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wakes up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then fasts. “So we came to Marwan and I informed him of what they had said, but their disagreement intensified for him. Fearing that Abu Hurairah might be telling him on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Marwan said to Abd al-Rahman, “I have determined for you when I came to him and told him: Can you help the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrate this? He said: No, but so-and-so and so-and-so told me, so I returned to Marwan. So she told him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2882","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Abdul told me. Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, heard Abu Hurairah say: Whoever becomes junub should not fast, so Abu Bakr set off, and his father Abdul-Rahman until they went to Umm Salamah and Aisha, and both of them said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to spend the morning in a state of ritual impurity, then fast.” So they went to Abu Hurairah and told him. He said: Did they say it to you? They said: Yes. He said: They know best. Al-Fadl ibn Abbas only informed him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Bakr. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I have no knowledge, but an informant told me about it."
"2883","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, on the authority of Malik, saying: Sumayy told me, that he heard Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, saying: My father and I were with Marwan bin Al-Hakam, who was the governor of the city, and it was reported that Abu Hurairah said: Whoever becomes junub has broken his fast. Today, Marwan said: I swear to you, O Abdul Rahman, that you will go to the mother of the believers, Aisha, and Umm Salamah, about that, so he went. Abdul-Rahman and I went with him, until we entered upon Aisha, and Abdul-Rahman greeted her and said: O Mother of the Believers, we were with Marwan, and it was mentioned to him that Abu Hurairah said: Whoever becomes junub will break his fast that day. Aisha said: “I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, if he was to wake up in the morning after having intercourse without a wet dream, then he should fast that day.” Then we left and entered Umm Salamah. So he asked her, and she said: As Aisha said, so we left until we came to Marwan, and Abd al-Rahman mentioned to him what they had said. Marwan said: I swore. It is upon you, O Abu Muhammad, to ride my animal, for it is at the gate. So go to Abu Hurairah, for he is on his land with aqeeq, so inform him. That is, Abu Bakr said: So Abd al-Rahman rode and I rode with him, until we came to Abu Hurairah, and Abd al-Rahman spoke with him for an hour, then It was mentioned to him, and Abu Hurairah said: I have no knowledge, but an informant told me about it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith said that he informed Abu Hurairah about the words of Aisha and Umm Salamah, and he said: This is how I calculated, and he did not attribute it to Sunday (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2884","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul-Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith, that Abu Hurairah used to say: Whoever is in a state of ritual impurity in the morning should break his fast, so Marwan sent to Aisha, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning when he was not having intercourse without a dream, then he would fast.” Then he came to Umm Salamah, and she said: He used to fast in the morning. junub, then fast, so Marwan came and informed him of the saying: Umm Salamah and Aisha, so he said: Go to Abu Hurairah, so he came to him and informed him According to the words of Umm Salamah and Aisha, he said: This is what I thought, and the wording: by Ibn al-Muthanna. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Khaled sent him Bin Abdullah and Abdul Aziz (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2885","Zakaria ibn Yahya told me, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiya told me, he said: Khaled informed, on the authority of Khalid, meaning the shoe, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would wake up fasting.”"
"2886","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Kamil told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, On the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, and then complete his fast.” Ayoub dissented from him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2887","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of 19 some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream and fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2888","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Abdul-Wahhab told us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He used to wake up in the morning without intercourse, then fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Iyad disagreed with them, and he narrated it, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith said that he sent Dhakwan to Aisha and asked her, and Nafi’ to Umm Salamah, so they returned to him and informed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2889","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah reported, saying: My father told me, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of the servant of his Lord. On the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, he said: Marwan sent me to Aisha, so I went to her and met her servant, Dhakwan. So I sent him to her to ask her about that, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning without intercourse while fasting, then fast.” It does not break the fast.” So I went to Marwan and told him about it, so he sent me to Umm Salamah. I went to her and found her servant Nafi’, so I sent him to her. So he asked her about that, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity while fasting, then he would fast and not break his fast.”"
"2890","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Amr bin Issa told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu Iyadh, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, that Marwan bin al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah, and he said: So I met her servant and sent him to her, and he asked her. Then he returned to him and informed him that she had told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had He is fasting in the morning while junub, then fasting in the morning.” Then he came to Aisha and said: I met her servant Dhakwan, so I sent him to her and he asked her, then he returned to him. He informed him that she had told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning after having intercourse without a wet dream, and then he would fast in the morning.” Then he came to Marwan and spoke to him. He said: I swear to you that you will go to Abu Hurairah and tell him about them. So he came to him and told him. He said: They know best"
"2891","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah reported, saying: Abu Haywa told us, saying: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He informed me Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, that his father Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith informed Marwan bin Al-Hakam that his mother Salamah and Aisha, the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was approaching dawn while he was near... his family, then he bathes and fasts.” The disagreement over Al-Zuhri was mentioned in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2892","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of His father, Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Umm Salamah and Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “dawn would overtake him while he was near his family, then he washes and fasts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2893","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Al-Layth, who is Ibn Saad, told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, said: Aisha told me, and Umm Salamah was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. “Fajr overtakes him while he is with some of his family, then he washes himself and fasts that day.” Qutayba bin Sa’id disagreed with him."
"2894","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Harith bin Hisham said: Aisha and Umm Salamah told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was approaching dawn while he was near the his family, then he washes and fasts.”"
"2895","Nasr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Ala reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham said: My father and I went to see Aisha and Umm Salamah, and they said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity and then fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2896","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim reported, saying: Bakr told us, on the authority of Isa, saying: Muhammad, who is the son of Abi Laila, told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha and Hafsa, that they said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dawn overtakes him while he is with his family, then he completes his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2897","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, and then that would not prevent him from fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2898","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, that Aisha said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to catch the dawn in Ramadan while he was junub and not dreaming, so he would bathe and then fast. “Mention of the disagreement over Arak bin Malik about it"
"2899","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr bin Mudar told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, On the authority of Arak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he used to say: “Who “Dawn came to him, and he was in a state of junub state, so he would not fast.” He was informed of that on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Abu Bakr Abd al-Rahman, so he informed Abd. The Most Gracious Marwan, and Marwan said to Abd al-Rahman, “I have determined that you should not ask Aisha and Umm Salamah about that.” So he asked them, and they said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity, then fast. “Abd al-Rahman informed Marwan of that, and he said: I have determined to meet you. Abu Hurairah, so I told him, and Abdul Rahman said to Marwan: I am afraid that he will say: He will follow my words. He said: I have appointed you, so Abdul met him. The Most Merciful found a land of his near Al-Juhfah, so he informed him. Abu Hurairah said: Al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed me about that."
"2900","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abd al-Wahhab told us, saying: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: Arak bin Malik informed me, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Abi Bakr, that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to go in the morning with a group of women.” Without a wet dream, then he fasts in the morning.” Mention of the disagreement over Yahya bin Sa’id regarding it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2901","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Yahya ibn Saeed, about a fight, then he mentioned a word that meant it, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abu Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without dreaming, and then continue fasting.” \Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak followed him (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2902","Muhammad ibn Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Arak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abu Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning when he was junub without dreaming, then fast.” That day “the disagreement over Solomon” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2903","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told me, he said: Khaled bin Mukhlid told me, he said: Sulayman told me, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, he said: Arak bin Malik told me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, To wake up in the morning with his wives without a dream, then fast in the morning.”"
"2904","Issa bin Hammad reported, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “He becomes junub without a dream, then fasts.”"
"2905","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Suleiman bin Muhammad Al-Mubaraki told us, he said: Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to spend the morning with some of his wives without A wet dream, then he should bathe and complete his fast.” Abu Al-Zubayr disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2906","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud reported, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, saying: Bakr bin Mudar reported, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, that Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “ In the morning he is devoid of his wives, then he completes that fast.”"
"2907","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Othman bin Saleh told us, he said: Bakr bin Mudar told me, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salama, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning with his wives, and then He will complete his fast on that day.” The disagreement over Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id bin Qais was mentioned in this hadith."
"2908","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading of it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha and Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning while having sexual intercourse.” A wet dream during Ramadan, then fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2909","Ahmad ibn al-Haytham, the judge of al-Thaghr, reported: Harmala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr told me, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh He is Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b Al-Himyari, that Abu Bakr told him, that Marwan sent him to Umm Salamah, asking On the authority of a man who was in a state of ritual impurity and then fasted. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would break his fast in the morning after having intercourse without a dream, then he would not break his fast or He decides"
"2910","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, saying: I heard Khaled, meaning Ibn Zayd, Abu Abdul-Rahman al-Shami, saying: I asked Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman as he was circumambulating the Kaaba. I said: Tell me about what I asked Aisha about, and Marwan ibn al-Hakam had sent him to him. Then he said, Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wake up in the morning after having intercourse without a dream, and thus complete his fast.” Mention of the disagreement over Mujahid in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2911","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, he said: Ubaidah, who is Ibn Humaid, told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith said: Abu Hurairah said: Whoever becomes junub has no fast for him, so Marwan sent Abd The Most Gracious went to Aisha and asked her, and he said to her: Abu Hurairah says: Whoever becomes junub has no fasting, so Aisha said: He has The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to avoid fasting and then complete his fast,” so he sent to Abu Hurairah and informed him that Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to avoid ritual impurity and then complete his fast.” Abu Hurairah refrained from doing so. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2912","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Dawud bin Rashid told us, he said: Abu Hafs told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning while he was in a state of ritual impurity and complete his fast.” The disagreement over Amer al-Shabi on this matter was mentioned. Hadith"
"2913","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Amer told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, he said I came to Aisha and said: Abu Hurairah says: Whoever becomes junub in the morning should not fast. She said: I was saying something about that. The caller calls for prayer, and he is in a state of junab, so I see the pool of water between his shoulders, then he prays the dawn prayer, then he continues to fast.” Mu’tamar ibn Sulaiman disagreed with him. They narrated it, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi. Zakaria bin Yahya told me. He said: Abu Hafs told us, he said: Mu’tamar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abd The Most Gracious, he said: So I mentioned it to Yahya, and he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Amer narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, and I heard Yahya saying: I heard Mujalid speaking, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, By the same token"
"2914","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Sulayman al-Shaybani told us He said: Al-Sha’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, he said: Abu Hurairah said: Whoever becomes junub So he does not fast, so my father went to Aisha, and I went in with him and he asked her, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning without He has a wet dream and fasts on that day.” So I mentioned that to Marwan, and he said: I called upon you when I met Abu Hurairah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2915","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Dawud informed, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham said that his father sent to Aisha asking her about the state of ritual impurity. Should he fast in the morning? She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would wake up in the morning obediently, not under compulsion, so he would wash and pray, and complete his fast that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2916","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad reported, saying: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha She said: “Bilal used to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and give him the call to prayer for the morning prayer while he was in a state of ritual ablution, and he would wash himself, then come to the mosque.” So he prays the two rak’ahs while his head is dripping from impurity, then he fasts that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2917","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, he said: Abu Abbad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar told me, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then he would wash himself, then he would go out to prayer, and he prays and I hear its recitation, then he fasts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2918","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Amr bin Aoun told us, he said: Khaled reported, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, getting up from the hairdryer, then completing his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2919","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told me, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “He should go out with his head dripping for the Fajr prayer, then complete his fast that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2920","Abu Bakr bin Hafs reported, on the authority of Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to get up from the washing machine for the morning prayer, wash himself, and then fast that day. Mutarrif differed from them and narrated it. On the authority of Al-Shaabi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha"
"2921","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Shabi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace. He spent the night in a state of ritual impurity, and Bilal came to him and called him to prayer, so he jumped up and poured water on his head, then he left and his head was flowing from the state of ritual impurity. Then he fasts that day of his.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sayyar sent him, and he narrated it on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2922","Yaqoub bin Mahan reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Sayyar reported, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to wash himself after dawn, then lead the people in prayer while dripping water on his head, then he would fast that day.” Asim continued him in his message."
"2923","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Amr bin Issa told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Aisha narrated, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would become fasting.” Mention of the difference On Suleiman bin Mihran Al-Amash in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2924","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abu Muawiyah reported, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then he would wash and fast that day.”"
"2925","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out to the dawn prayer and his head was Let him drip water and then continue fasting that day.”"
"2926","Zakaria bin Yahya told me again, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, and Jami’ bin Shaddad, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out to pray and his head was dripping Then he continues to fast that day.” The disagreement over Al-Hakam bin Utaiba was mentioned in this hadith."
"2927","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal told us, he said: I heard Al-Hakam bin Utaiba. He narrates, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, who said: I entered upon Aisha, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God bless him and grant him peace, he would go out to pray in the morning, and his head would drip from his washing, then he would fast in the morning.” My father mentioned it to Marwan, and he said: You should go to Abu Hurairah until you inform him. Abu Hurairah said: It is as Aisha said."
"2928","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, He said: I went to see Aisha, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then he would wash himself and then go to the mosque in the morning.” And he would drip his head, then he would fast that day.” So I told Marwan what she said, and he said to me: Tell me, meaning Abu Hurairah, what Aisha said, So I said: He is a friend of mine, and I would like you to spare me. He said: I bequeathed to you, so he and I went to him and told him what she said, and he said: Aisha, then I know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the disagreement over Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2929","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without being able to do so, and then fast.”"
"2930","Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Sulayman told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Amr, who is Al-Awza’i, told us, He said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Aisha and Umm Salamah used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning while avoiding intercourse without a dream, then he would fast.”"
"2931","Ahmad ibn Harb reported, saying: Asbat told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Abu Hurairah said: Whoever the dawn reaches him While he was in a state of impurity, let him break his fast. The people were terrified by what Abu Hurairah said, so Marwan, who was the governor of the city, sent Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, so he said: Go to your aunt Umm Salamah and ask her about this hadith that Abu Hurairah narrated, so he came to her and mentioned that. To her, she said: I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would wake up in the morning beside me, then fast and order me to fast in Ramadan.” So Marwan said: Tell him this hadith that Umm Salamah told you. So he came to him and mentioned that to him. Abu Hurairah said: So-and-so told us. The opposite of him was narrated by Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, who narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman bin Hatib. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2932","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, saying: Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah, that Abu Hurairah used to narrate: Whoever catches dawn while he is junub, then do not He fasts, so Marwan said to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith: Abu Hurairah is narrating a hadith that has alarmed us, so go to Umm Salamah and ask her. About that, he went to Umm Salamah and asked her about that. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to wake up in the morning with me and fast.” And he commands me to fast.” So he returned to Marwan and told him about that. Marwan said to him: Go to Abu Hurairah and tell him about that. So he went to him, and he mentioned to him that Marwan had ordered him to go to Umm Salama and ask her about that. He said: So I went to her and asked her, Then I went to him and told him, and he ordered me to come to you and inform you. Then I told him what Umm Salamah had told me, and Abu Hurairah said: No. You have to say that Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated to me, mentioning the disagreement over Sulaiman bin Yasar in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2933","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, he said: Khathim bin Arak bin Malik told us, he said: he told me Suleiman bin Yassar said: I heard Aisha say: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then he would wash and fast that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2934","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala al-San’ani reported, saying: Khalid bin al-Harith told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Yasar said: I went to see Umm Salamah and she told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, and then \fasts\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2935","Amr bin Ali reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, who said: Sulayman bin Yasar told me, on the authority of Umm Salama, who said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to touch his family at night, and in the morning he would be in a state of ritual impurity, then he would wash and fast. “The disagreement over Aflah ibn Praiseworthy in Him"
"2936","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Aflah bin Humaid told me, that Al-Qasim bin Muhammad told him, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited his family, then fell asleep and did not wash, until In the morning, he took a bath, prayed, and then fasted that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2937","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani reported, on the authority of Hammad bin Khalid, on the authority of Aflah bin Humaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “He visited some of his wives, then he slept until morning, and he bathed while he was in a state of ritual impurity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2938","Ayoub bin Muhammad al-Ruqqi al-Wazzan told me, he said: Omar bin Ayyub told us, he said: Aflah told us, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had intercourse with some of his wives, then he slept until morning, then he took a bath and completed his fast,” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: The first is more correct: the narration of Ibn Wahb and Hammad bin Khalid. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2939","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya, the judge of Damascus, told me, on the authority of Abu Amir, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He had intercourse with some of his wives, then he slept and did not wash himself until he woke up in the morning, so he washed and prayed, then completed his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2940","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Abu Asim al-Nabil told us, and I asked him, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning during a state of ritual impurity and then fast.” He mentioned the hadith of Ata’ on the authority of Aisha in which (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2941","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would fast that day.” \that\"""""
"2942","Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Kufi Al-Masruqi told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Ata bin Abi Rabah told us On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would fast.” Narrated by Al-Qasim bin Zakaria, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abdul Malik (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2943","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afflicted with ritual impurity during the night, and he wanted to fast. He would sleep, wake up, and become junub in the morning. of water upon him and completes his fast.”"
"2944","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, saying: Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik. And Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam reported, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afflicted with impurity during the night when he wanted to fast, so he would sleep, wake up, and wake up in the morning. Water and completes his fast.” The disagreement over Hammad bin Abi Suleiman was mentioned in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2945","Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed told us, Ka’b bin Abdullah Basri told us, and he was trustworthy, he said: He told us Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day in Ramadan, and his head was He dripped from intercourse, so he continued his fast that day.”"
"2946","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abu Al-Nadr told us, on the authority of Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go out at dawn with his head dripping, and then he would continue fasting.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more likely to be true than the hadith of Ka’b, and Ka’b bin Abdullah we do not know, and his hadith is wrong, and Zaydah is more proven than Abu Asim. Among the hadiths of al-Nadr, the hadith of al-Nadr is more likely to be correct. It was followed on this narration by Mughirah bin Maqsim. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2947","Abu Bakr bin Hafs Basri reported, on the authority of Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to get up from the washing machine for the morning prayer, wash himself, and then fast.” Narrated by Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha"
"2948","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Sharik reported, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out For the dawn prayer, with his head dripping from the ritual ablution of ritual impurity, then he fasts that day.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Abu Yunus, On the authority of Aisha, without this wording (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2949","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Ismail told us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman told us, that Abu Yunus was Aisha’s client. He told him, on the authority of Aisha, a man who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while she was listening from behind the door, and he said: O Messenger of God, will you overtake me? Praying while I am in a state of ritual impurity, so should I fast? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And prayer overtakes me while I am in a state of ritual impurity, so I fast.” He said: You are not like us, O Messenger of God. God has forgiven me. For you, whatever your previous sins and what will be later, he said: “By God, I hope that I will be the most fearful of God and the most knowledgeable of you in what I fear.” Mention of a hadith Amer bin Abi Umayyah on the authority of Umm Salamah in it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2950","Humayd ibn Masada Basri reported, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, On the authority of Aamir bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the morning in a state of ritual impurity, then he would become fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2951","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out to the morning prayer with his head dripping and then he would fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2952","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out to pray and his head was dripping. \fasting\"""""
"2953","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Malik told us, on the authority of Sumayy, Abu Bakr’s client, on the authority of his client, Abu Bakr, on the authority of a man from the Prophet’s companions, who prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “fasting while traveling, pouring water on his head because of the intense heat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2954","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah Al-Ghaylani Al-Basri reported, saying: Abu Amer told us, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari said that he heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have commanded them.” \With the siwak\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2955","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym al-Dimashqi reported, saying: Marwan, who is al-Fazari, told us: Muhammad, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman, told us. Ibn Mahran, he said: Saeed Ibn Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “If it had not been a burden on my nation, I would have imposed the siwak.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2956","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu al-Numan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman al-Sarraj, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abu Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have imposed on them the siwak with all “Ablution,” Hammad said, and I heard it from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar."
"2957","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered the use of the siwak at every ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2958","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, Saeed told him, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"
"2959","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Abdul Wahhab told us, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered the use of the siwak at every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2960","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered the use of the siwak at every prayer.”"
"2961","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak along with ablution.”"
"2962","Amr bin Uthman reported, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have imposed on them the siwak along with ablution,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Error"
"2963","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for the people, I would have ordered them to perform ablution at every prayer and to use the siwak after ablution.”"
"2964","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ataa, a servant Umm Sabiya, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak at every turn.” \prayer\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2965","Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman: Yahya al-Qattan used to say: Muhammad ibn Amr is more sound than Muhammad ibn Ishaq in hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2966","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “If it were not that it would be difficult for the believers, I would have ordered them to use the siwak at every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2967","Muhammad bin Yahya reported, saying: Bishr bin Umar told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak with every ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2968","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he used to say: “If it were not that it would be difficult for his nation, he would have commanded them to use the siwak with every prayer or every ablution.”"
"2969","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, saying: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he used to say: “If it were not that it would be difficult for his nation, he would have ordered them to use the siwak with every prayer or every ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2970","Muhammad ibn Mansour al-Makki reported on the permissibility, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Abu al-Zannad told us, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to delay the evening prayer and to use the siwak at every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
